omxvideodec: only flag header subframes as codec config

h264parse/h265parse set GST_BUFFER_FLAG_HEADER on the access unit that carries
SPS/PPS, which also holds the IDR slice. In au alignment that whole frame was
sent with OMX_BUFFERFLAG_CODECCONFIG, but OpenMAX says codec config buffers
carry only config data. CedarC asserts on codec config larger than 20 KiB and
aborts on the first keyframe. Header-only buffers only exist in subframe mode.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
diff -ru a/omx/gstomxvideodec.c b/omx/gstomxvideodec.c
--- a/omx/gstomxvideodec.c	2026-11-10 03:47:15.680465614 +0100
+++ b/omx/gstomxvideodec.c	2026-11-10 03:47:15.691449684 +0100
@@ -3204,7 +3204,9 @@
     if (first_ouput_buffer && GST_VIDEO_CODEC_FRAME_IS_SYNC_POINT (frame))
       buf->omx_buf->nFlags |= OMX_BUFFERFLAG_SYNCFRAME;
 
-    if (header)
+    /* only subframes are header-only, a whole au flagged header still
+     * carries picture data and must not be sent as codec config */
+    if (header && subframe_mode)
       buf->omx_buf->nFlags |= OMX_BUFFERFLAG_CODECCONFIG;
 
     /* TODO: Set flags
